00:01:00.631 --> 00:01:01.714
- Yeah.

00:01:01.714 --> 00:01:05.150
- He just built a moat the other day.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.613
- Wow that's just somebody

00:01:06.613 --> 00:01:08.255
that is so rich that's just bored.

00:01:08.255 --> 00:01:10.952
- It's like come on
brother is that a falcon?

00:01:10.952 --> 00:01:12.520
What do you have in front of your house?

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.433
- It's a phoenix!

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:14.983
- It's a phoenix and I
thought it'd be great.

00:01:14.983 --> 00:01:18.687
- And it lights up, there's fire involved.

00:01:18.687 --> 00:01:20.244
I know, I drive though some neighborhoods,

00:01:20.244 --> 00:01:21.475
and people are crazy here.

00:01:21.475 --> 00:01:24.449
- He's got a hologram
mailman, that's not even real.

00:01:24.449 --> 00:01:25.713
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:25.713 --> 00:01:26.873
- "Put the mail here."

00:01:26.873 --> 00:01:29.408
Well what kinda neighborhood
did you grow up in?

00:01:29.408 --> 00:01:30.877
- I remember my childhood

00:01:30.877 --> 00:01:33.897
from being in a little town
called Caruthersville, Missouri.

00:01:33.897 --> 00:01:35.244
You get "What?"

00:01:35.244 --> 00:01:36.088
- What?

00:01:36.088 --> 00:01:39.553
- Again, a small city southeast Missouri,

00:01:39.553 --> 00:01:41.019
so it was that kinda neighborhood where

00:01:41.019 --> 00:01:43.586
you didn't do much, there wasn't games

00:01:43.586 --> 00:01:46.861
so like to have fun your neighbors,

00:01:46.861 --> 00:01:49.255
we would throw rocks at
each other as a game.

00:01:49.255 --> 00:01:50.683
- We did that as a kid.

00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:51.611
- It was fun, it was a game.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.402
- Yeah, which seems kind of
abusive now that we're adults.

00:01:53.402 --> 00:01:55.776
- It was very abusive
but yo with the shoe.

00:01:55.776 --> 00:01:56.760
(yelling)

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.593
Oh, you almost got me!

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:01.922
- You're supposed to play dodge ball

00:02:01.922 --> 00:02:03.477
with an actual dodge ball.

00:02:03.477 --> 00:02:04.910
- Right but no rocks was it.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:06.216
- We did that too.

00:02:06.216 --> 00:02:08.653
- But it was great because you go outside,

00:02:08.653 --> 00:02:10.769
you race everywhere.

00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:11.602
- Right.

00:02:11.602 --> 00:02:12.436
- You race everywhere.

00:02:12.436 --> 00:02:14.279
- And tag sounds like hell now.

00:02:14.279 --> 00:02:17.121
- With this weather no way.

00:02:17.121 --> 00:02:18.265
- Yeah.

00:02:18.265 --> 00:02:19.930
My kids are like "No
you want to play tag?"

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.906
I'm like "No I'm 37 girl
I'm gon' to sit right here."

00:02:21.906 --> 00:02:22.739
- Right.

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:23.572
- You play tag.

00:02:23.572 --> 00:02:24.405
- Yeah.

00:02:24.405 --> 00:02:26.753
- Wear it out before bedtime.

00:02:26.753 --> 00:02:29.580
- Hide and seek would be like
go, hide, all right good.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.537
- I know my husband and I are like--

00:02:31.537 --> 00:02:33.406
- You're a winner, wherever you are.

00:02:33.406 --> 00:02:36.156
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:39.123 --> 00:02:40.635
- Play in traffic you're fine.

00:02:40.635 --> 00:02:41.751
- You're fine, you're great.

00:02:41.751 --> 00:02:43.751
- So what's it like when you go back home?

00:02:43.751 --> 00:02:45.812
Are they excited that you're super famous

00:02:45.812 --> 00:02:46.738
or do they not care?

00:02:46.738 --> 00:02:48.001
My family doesn't care.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.120
- No they care because you're usually

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.586
gonna come back in with some
good gifts or something.

00:02:52.586 --> 00:02:53.426
- Yeah.

00:02:53.426 --> 00:02:54.558
- That's the main thing
but after that part

00:02:54.558 --> 00:02:56.066
then it's like you're back regular.

00:02:56.066 --> 00:02:58.181
But I think that's a big
thing about going home

00:02:58.181 --> 00:03:02.500
is that's the expectation of
who you know and who you met.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.387
- It's not really you, it's
who they can know via you.

00:03:04.387 --> 00:03:07.153
- Yeah it's not even about
me they like oh, y'know,

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.835
they call me Tony, that's
my at home name, Tony.

00:03:09.835 --> 00:03:10.678
- I love it.

00:03:10.678 --> 00:03:11.996
I want an at home name.

00:03:11.996 --> 00:03:12.982
- So then it's like "What's Denzel like?"

00:03:12.982 --> 00:03:14.305
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:14.305 --> 00:03:15.810
- Wait have you met, what is Denzel like?

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.278
Wait, I love Denzel!

00:03:17.278 --> 00:03:18.958
- Kelly knows he's a star.

00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:20.509
(laughing)

00:03:20.509 --> 00:03:23.375
- I'm like wait, I
could watch those movies

00:03:23.375 --> 00:03:24.784
all the time, "The Equalizer."

00:03:24.784 --> 00:03:25.624
- Yeah "The Equalizer"
good right, he's bad.

00:03:25.624 --> 00:03:26.737
- He is crazy, yes it's so good.

00:03:26.737 --> 00:03:27.570
- Yeah I want to be that bad

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.204
- Me too, me too.

00:03:29.204 --> 00:03:31.059
Well on "The Neighborhood" you have,

00:03:31.059 --> 00:03:31.892
on your show "The Neighborhood"

00:03:31.892 --> 00:03:33.711
you have a thing called a yardacue?

00:03:33.711 --> 00:03:34.701
- Yeah.
- What is that?

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:38.607
- Well this is something we
had to do for television,

00:03:38.607 --> 00:03:41.473
but basically do get a
barbecue in the front yard,

00:03:41.473 --> 00:03:43.202
and actually it's
actually all about getting

00:03:43.202 --> 00:03:44.560
people to come and be a part of it.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.782
Usually people barbecue in their backyards

00:03:46.782 --> 00:03:49.160
and it's only invited guests but when you

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.927
do a yardacue you do it in the front yard

00:03:50.927 --> 00:03:53.321
and it's more like a
block party it's more like

00:03:53.321 --> 00:03:54.555
people welcome to come.

00:03:54.555 --> 00:03:56.556
- That's fun, that's really cool.

00:03:56.556 --> 00:03:59.403
- Some just stop by have a
good time at the yardacue.

00:03:59.403 --> 00:04:01.301
- Do you ever have people though

00:04:01.301 --> 00:04:02.196
where you're like "Bye."

00:04:02.196 --> 00:04:04.053
- [Cedric] Well sure.

00:04:04.053 --> 00:04:05.937
- Wait you aren't invited.

00:04:05.937 --> 00:04:07.721
- Yeah you don't want to
get people who mix it up

00:04:07.721 --> 00:04:09.054
for a yard sale.

00:04:10.328 --> 00:04:12.240
"What about these chairs?"

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.806
Like no we using these bro.

00:04:13.806 --> 00:04:14.924
- I'll give you five dollars.

00:04:14.924 --> 00:04:17.128
- Yeah "I'll give you five
dollars for the grill."

00:04:17.128 --> 00:04:20.211
No it's a brisket on there right now.

00:04:21.706 --> 00:04:23.953
- I totally grew up with
garage sales as well.

00:04:23.953 --> 00:04:25.205
- Oh all right.

00:04:25.205 --> 00:04:26.694
- I heard that you're now a grandpa,

00:04:26.694 --> 00:04:27.527
